## compose_new design (agreed)
- GET /compose: blank form (To, Subject, body). POST /compose sends.
- No mail.raw, no find_entry/generate_raw/derive_reply_fields.
- Same payload as reply minus the "headers" block; same send_json.sh
  subprocess call as /reply POST.
- Open question: address entry on a T9A keypad. Start with plain
  typing; later, a recent-contacts list built from headers.txt.
- Don't extract shared helpers until real duplication exists.

## Known gaps
- Non-multipart messages with base64 bodies are not decoded.
- Read-flag sync deliberately not implemented (see handover v3).
- map/ and drive/ code is not in GitHub. Before committing, check
  their config files for keys and gitignore data files (favs,
  recent.json, request/response.json).
- Housekeeping: README is stale (describes msmtp); appbak.py and
  mail_app_merged.py are stale; delete ~/Mail/INBOX.old,
  ~/.mbsync/state.old, ~/.mbsyncrc.bak after a few healthy days.

